1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Solar cells convert light energy into electrical energy.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Panels produce DC electricity. An inverter converts it to AC for household use.

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:36,000
DC maintains a direction of current. AC periodically reverses direction.

4
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:45,000
At constant power, two kilowatts for three hours gives six kilowatt-hours.

5
00:00:45,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Light becomes DC electricity. Inverters provide AC. Energy depends on power and time.
